          "versionNonce": 1731855631,
          "isDeleted": false,
          "boundElements": [],
          "updated": 1788120863381,
          "link": null,
          "locked": false,
          "text": "Salmon swim upstream to reproduce at the same location where they were born, because if\nthat environment was safe for them, it should also be a safe place for their offspring.However,\ndams can block salmon from traveling upstream, preventing them from reaching their\nspawning grounds. This means fewer new salmon will be born while the older salmon die off,\ncausing the salmon population to slowly decrease.A decline in the salmon population can\naffect the entire ecosystem. Salmon are a major food source for bears, so if there are fewer\nsalmon, the bear population may also decrease. If there are fewer bears, they will hunt fewer\nother animals, causing the populations of those animals to grow. As the populations of larger\nanimals increase, they may eat more of the smaller animals, causing the smaller animals'\npopulations to decrease or even disappear.Eventually, the larger animals may run out of food\nas their prey become scarce.Their populations could then decrease as well. Meanwhile, some\nsmaller animals that feed on plants could increase in number and consume too many plants. If\ntoo much vegetation is eaten, there may not be enough plants left to support those animals,\ncausing their populations to decline too.This shows how one change, such as dams preventing\nsalmon from reaching their spawning grounds, can have a major effect on an entire ecosystem.\n    Fish ladders are structures built next to dams that help fish, such as salmon, travel\nupstream to reach their spawning grounds. They work by creating a series of smaller steps or\npools that allow fish to move around the dam instead of being blocked by it. Fish ladders are\nimportant because they help salmon reach the places where they were born so they can\nreproduce and keep the population healthy. By allowing salmon to continue their natural\nmigration, fish ladders can also help protect the animals and ecosystems that depend on\nsalmon for food. However it expensive and hard to construct and it always releases water\neven if there are no fish.\n",
          "fontSize": 63.397418212500895,
          "fontFamily": 6,
          "textAlign": "left",
          "verticalAlign": "top",
          "containerId": null,
          "originalText": "Salmon swim upstream to reproduce at the same location where they were born, because if that environment was safe for them, it should also be a safe place for their offspring.However, dams can block salmon from traveling upstream, preventing them from reaching their spawning grounds. This means fewer new salmon will be born while the older salmon die off, causing the salmon population to slowly decrease.A decline in the salmon population can affect the entire ecosystem. Salmon are a major food source for bears, so if there are fewer salmon, the bear population may also decrease. If there are fewer bears, they will hunt fewer other animals, causing the populations of those animals to grow. As the populations of larger animals increase, they may eat more of the smaller animals, causing the smaller animals' populations to decrease or even disappear.Eventually, the larger animals may run out of food as their prey become scarce.Their populations could then decrease as well. Meanwhile, some smaller animals that feed on plants could increase in number and consume too many plants. If too much vegetation is eaten, there may not be enough plants left to support those animals, causing their populations to decline too.This shows how one change, such as dams preventing salmon from reaching their spawning grounds, can have a major effect on an entire ecosystem.\n    Fish ladders are structures built next to dams that help fish, such as salmon, travel upstream to reach their spawning grounds. They work by creating a series of smaller steps or pools that allow fish to move around the dam instead of being blocked by it. Fish ladders are important because they help salmon reach the places where they were born so they can reproduce and keep the population healthy. By allowing salmon to continue their natural migration, fish ladders can also help protect the animals and ecosystems that depend on salmon for food. However it expensive and hard to construct and it always releases water even if there are no fish.\n",
